#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119577 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/assets/2a24a49f0fc47c235776597df655e75be9c68cffbb7988db16b36d9200f801bc.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ff1b670-d9ce-578f-abed-beb705375599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338725} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f5a6ad-f90e-57b3-9d8a-f1d55a9c1f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338726} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6729de-aff7-5c4c-98ad-1bb06eb79a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338727} {:answer/id #uuid "eac8ebca-c530-5195-acb2-b6292ade13da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338728} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6b7658-2157-5f1b-b131-5b91d1e140f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-8,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d6729de-aff7-5c4c-98ad-1bb06eb79a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338727} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f06fdb5-06f0-5457-8b29-4b3079bc722a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d28c265-18d6-5656-afcf-7f8222829274" :question/math-academy-id "q-108311" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,-2,3⟩+t⟨0,3,-1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩=-7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ ⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ 5+3(-2+3t)+(-2)(3-t) & =-7 \\\\ 5-6+9t-6+2t & =-7 \\\\ 11t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5,-2+3(0),3-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,-2,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad1f5c5e-9bfc-542f-b83d-9cd12da5c2e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338732} {:answer/id #uuid "031f0ab7-98e5-5ef1-b694-26f424e0c1fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338733} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0767ba-c8fe-5d02-98cb-a2daad8cd428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338734} {:answer/id #uuid "b90c5c3a-2f79-5901-856b-ccae222540c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338735} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e8c10b-4c6c-548e-8a40-af66b3fc3888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad1f5c5e-9bfc-542f-b83d-9cd12da5c2e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338732} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd20147-884b-5aad-8617-b8c00cdeb58e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aae7d446-6165-5274-a5d2-5622980a25ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-108313" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-1⟩+t⟨5,-2,4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩=22.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ 0(3+5t)+1(-2t)+(-2)(-1+4t) & =22 \\\\ -2t+2-8t & =22 \\\\ -10t & =20 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-2),-2(-2),-1+4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,4,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-7,4,-9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0685c34e-7f8c-542c-a8df-082d2bd2d0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338753} {:answer/id #uuid "0ebcf735-1d00-575e-9786-8bd7db6f13d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,13,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338754} {:answer/id #uuid "9c7549da-aa05-5f9a-b970-554a5ae24af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338755} {:answer/id #uuid "55bad4ad-1cc1-5384-974a-a376f90f80bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338756} {:answer/id #uuid "4847ee0f-9e5c-5369-bbda-8d74f3fffe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,-1,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0685c34e-7f8c-542c-a8df-082d2bd2d0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338753} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aabbaa0-da27-5e13-92cc-3d64261bc76d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36683b19-26fd-5526-a537-6298e5ac4183" :question/math-academy-id "q-108337" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815fabd4-9942-57b4-86bc-0a4e8ea26733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 0, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117493} {:answer/id #uuid "828a2813-0e1a-52fa-8e56-5675b46d6c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2, 19)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117494} {:answer/id #uuid "a16033ae-062f-5189-8043-5212bcbcca8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 7, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117495} {:answer/id #uuid "b4553fc5-f5f7-54cf-b55a-bad20dc70a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117496} {:answer/id #uuid "2d858785-175b-5493-a285-e2730b6169da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 3, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "815fabd4-9942-57b4-86bc-0a4e8ea26733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 0, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117493} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b7f63a-ddcb-5c41-8c61-f730276427a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117492}] :question/id #uuid "a9c8b702-f6a3-5488-9345-1b22f3aeec01" :question/math-academy-id "q-33081" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: \\frac{x - 1}{2} = \\frac{y + 2}{1} = \\frac{z - 1}{3}, Π: r \\cdot ⟨1, 6, 2⟩ = 19$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8977164a-8ad7-56e9-94a7-d1231f0c5ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9, 9, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117839} {:answer/id #uuid "fd122388-c8df-5ba9-8c16-8ce6fa095bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-1, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117840} {:answer/id #uuid "46f916f3-3853-57e9-ba4e-59cb01cf50fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117841} {:answer/id #uuid "670f3c35-0bae-5d98-a7f7-406e9c05c9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9, 7,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117842} {:answer/id #uuid "6812f233-b49b-50e7-80f8-912186dc94d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46f916f3-3853-57e9-ba4e-59cb01cf50fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117841} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efee06f-3bfd-5143-ad04-c2e4495511e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c755ffbb-8374-5c52-a967-a6387ef6da9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-33992" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5ac142-a41e-558b-94e2-54be6e32075e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338816} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdda2c9-4fe5-5bb2-9519-342c31cd32ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338817} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9408c3-0eb4-5b30-8808-98420723e10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338818} {:answer/id #uuid "105d22a0-f100-57a5-83c4-a6a5d8b76d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338819} {:answer/id #uuid "410b9713-26d7-5617-92d8-b56182622870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,21,-14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9408c3-0eb4-5b30-8808-98420723e10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338818} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7732099-3c9a-500e-a0a3-ab40ac1da9d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45a75007-267d-50a7-b554-5511306a0ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74003" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$"}]}
